!scriptcards {{ 

  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Script Name : Tim's Spiritual Weapon Mod for D&D 5E 2014
  --/| Version     : 2.0.0
  --/| Author      : Timothy Beasley
  --/| API Mods    : ScriptCards
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Automates Spiritual Weapon for the 2014 D&D 5E sheet.
  --/| Summons a configurable weapon token beside the caster and builds a token
  --/| action attack based on the spell slot used.
  --/| FEATURES:
  --/| * Weapon Library: 157 BG3 weapon tokens, plus miscellaneous token options.
  --/| * Spell Slot Support: Cast at 2nd through 9th level and deducts the slot.
  --/| * Scaling Attack: Updates the Spiritual Weapon attack for the chosen slot level.
  --/| * Token Customization: Save a random weapon, chosen weapon, custom image URL,
  --/|   and custom name on the SpiritualWeapon NPC mule.
  --/| * Spell Display: Shows the spell details with a settings gear and spellbook button.
  --/| SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
  --/| 1. Create a character named: ScriptCards_TemplateMule (for CSS).
  --/| 2. Create an NPC character named: SpiritualWeapon.
  --/| 3. Run the script once to initialize the templates and NPC action.
  --/| 4. Create a macro on the caster's sheet and enable "Show as Token Action."
  --/| 5. Select the caster's token and launch the macro to begin.
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --~|array;objects:character;TemplateID;ScriptCards_TemplateMule
  --?"[@TemplateID(0)]" -eq ""|[ --#title|Spiritual Weapon Setup --+|[c]Please make sure you've created a character called [b]ScriptCards_TemplateMule[/b][br] in your game journal. It has to be exactly this name and is case sensitive. [br]This is where the style information for Spiritual Weapon will be kept.[/c] --X| --]|
  --/| GET STYLE ABILITY ON TEMPLATE MULE CHARACTER AND CHECK IF FIRST RUN
  --~IsTemplate|system;findability;ScriptCards_TemplateMule;statblockv4public
  --?"[&IsTemplate]" -eq "AbilityNotFound"|[
    --+|[c]The style information has been written, please run the Mod again.[/c]
